{"id":"psc-human-resources-running-totals","tier":"OFFICIAL","title":"Contracting out approved each year, by Human Resources’ own running total","question":"How much work did City departments ask to contract out to private firms and nonprofits, in Human Resources’ own count?","finding":"Each packet from 2022-11-07 to 2024-07-15 carries Human Resources’ cost summary of the personal-services contracts it processed in the fiscal year to date. Fiscal 2022-23 reached $3.60 billion by the meeting of 2023-06-05; fiscal 2023-24 reached $4.45 billion by 2024-06-03, including $444.9 million it lists as expedited approvals. The largest single packets were 2023-07-17 ($1.63 billion), 2023-03-06 ($976.1 million), 2024-07-15 ($430.1 million). The packets after July 2024 stop printing the summary.","how":"The cover memo of each packet (“DHR has prepared the following cost summary”) prints three figures: the total of this report, the expedited approvals so far in the fiscal year, and the total for the fiscal year so far. They are read as printed, one row per meeting. Packets of one meeting that come in several parts are read together.","limits":"An approval sets a ceiling on what may be spent over the life of the contracts, often five years or more, and on construction-heavy requests it includes the whole construction budget (the Airport’s West Field request of July 2023 says so); it is not a year’s spending. Contracting out with the Commission’s approval is the route the Charter provides. Some packets for these years are not on disk, so the running total is read only where a packet carries it.","columns":[{"k":"meeting","t":"Meeting","type":"date"},{"k":"fy","t":"Fiscal year","type":"text"},{"k":"report","t":"This packet","type":"usd"},{"k":"expedited","t":"Expedited approvals so far this year","type":"usd"},{"k":"fyTotal","t":"Fiscal year so far","type":"usd"}],"rows":[{"meeting":"2024-07-15","fy":"2024-25","report":430144326,"expedited":15059000,"fyTotal":508589086},{"meeting":"